            "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tennis Elbow 4 is the successor to Tennis  Elbow 2013, acclaimed by many Steam reviewers as one of the most  realistic tennis simulations ever made.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >TE4  pushes the realism of tennis rallies even further with fully reworked  ball, strike and player physics. The game is built around anticipation,  positioning, player inertia, shot selection and risk management, while  still letting you start playing quickly with the right assists and  difficulty settings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Created by  and for tennis fans, Tennis Elbow 4 is a deep tennis simulation that  can be enjoyed at many levels. You can play casually with helpers such  as Auto-Positioning, Footwork Boost and Aiming Preview, or progressively  turn them down to experience a more demanding and precise game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Like  real tennis, TE4 rewards players who learn to read the ball, prepare  early, position themselves properly and choose the right shot under  pressure. The basics can click quickly, but mastering the rallies,  timing and movement gives the game its long-term depth.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To  beat your opponent, you can use all the main shots available on a real  court: safe strikes, accelerations, topspin shots, slices, drop shots,  lobs, volleys and smashes. Cross-court rallies, changes of rhythm,  defensive play and risky winners all emerge naturally from the physics  and the tactical situation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With  many difficulty levels and sublevels, Tennis Elbow 4 lets you tune the  challenge very precisely. Lower levels and assists are ideal to learn  the controls and enjoy the career at your own rhythm, while higher levels  bring the pace, pressure and consistency closer to professional tennis.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tennis  Elbow 4 features one of the most complete World Tours ever made in a  tennis game. With over 3500 players evolving across several decades and  more than 400 tournaments each year, from low-rank Junior events to  top-level Pro finals, in both singles and doubles, you can experience  the long-term progression of a real tennis career.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The  Tennis Elbow engine is also very open to modding, with many Mods  directly downloadable from within the game. Mods can add or improve  players, outfits, courts, sounds and many other elements, letting the  community push the game even further.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tennis Elbow 4  is made for players who want deep rallies, realistic ball physics,  meaningful positioning and a true learning curve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features:</strong> </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >9 different court surfaces : clay, green clay, grass, hard, blue-green hard, classic synthetic, NewLine synthetic, indoor hard and indoor synthetic; each with a specific rebound </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >21 Stadiums around the world </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >400+ tournaments, with 3500+ players evolving over 70 years, from 1973 for men &amp; 1983 for women, to 2042 </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Commentaries by Tennis TV commentator Darren Kilfara </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Country Cup </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Singles &amp; doubles competitions </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Junior &amp; Pro Tours </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >6 difficulty levels, each split into 10 sublevels </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Full ranking system </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >3D male &amp; female players, fully customizable </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Singles, 3, and doubles games </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Split screen </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Network : LAN and online games </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1 to 6 games per set, in best of 1, 3 or 5 sets </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >7 camera modes </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Moving sun and Night session </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is very Modding-friendly</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Warnings for the Online mode :</strong> </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can play doubles with 4 human players on 1 computer, or on 2 computers with 2 players on each, via LAN or Internet — but not on four separate computers.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Online play uses peer-to-peer (P2P) connections with no relay server. This means that if you're behind CGNAT, or if you cannot forward a UDP port or use UPnP on your Internet router, you won’t be able to host a match. You should still be able to join a host, though.</p></li></ul>",
            "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tennis Elbow 4 is the successor to Tennis  Elbow 2013, acclaimed by many Steam reviewers as one of the most  realistic tennis simulations ever made.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >TE4  pushes the realism of tennis rallies even further with fully reworked  ball, strike and player physics. The game is built around anticipation,  positioning, player inertia, shot selection and risk management, while  still letting you start playing quickly with the right assists and  difficulty settings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Created by  and for tennis fans, Tennis Elbow 4 is a deep tennis simulation that  can be enjoyed at many levels. You can play casually with helpers such  as Auto-Positioning, Footwork Boost and Aiming Preview, or progressively  turn them down to experience a more demanding and precise game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Like  real tennis, TE4 rewards players who learn to read the ball, prepare  early, position themselves properly and choose the right shot under  pressure. The basics can click quickly, but mastering the rallies,  timing and movement gives the game its long-term depth.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To  beat your opponent, you can use all the main shots available on a real  court: safe strikes, accelerations, topspin shots, slices, drop shots,  lobs, volleys and smashes. Cross-court rallies, changes of rhythm,  defensive play and risky winners all emerge naturally from the physics  and the tactical situation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With  many difficulty levels and sublevels, Tennis Elbow 4 lets you tune the  challenge very precisely. Lower levels and assists are ideal to learn  the controls and enjoy the career at your own rhythm, while higher levels  bring the pace, pressure and consistency closer to professional tennis.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tennis  Elbow 4 features one of the most complete World Tours ever made in a  tennis game. With over 3500 players evolving across several decades and  more than 400 tournaments each year, from low-rank Junior events to  top-level Pro finals, in both singles and doubles, you can experience  the long-term progression of a real tennis career.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The  Tennis Elbow engine is also very open to modding, with many Mods  directly downloadable from within the game. Mods can add or improve  players, outfits, courts, sounds and many other elements, letting the  community push the game even further.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tennis Elbow 4  is made for players who want deep rallies, realistic ball physics,  meaningful positioning and a true learning curve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features:</strong> </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >9 different court surfaces : clay, green clay, grass, hard, blue-green hard, classic synthetic, NewLine synthetic, indoor hard and indoor synthetic; each with a specific rebound </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >21 Stadiums around the world </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >400+ tournaments, with 3500+ players evolving over 70 years, from 1973 for men &amp; 1983 for women, to 2042 </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Commentaries by Tennis TV commentator Darren Kilfara </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Country Cup </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Singles &amp; doubles competitions </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Junior &amp; Pro Tours </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >6 difficulty levels, each split into 10 sublevels </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Full ranking system </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >3D male &amp; female players, fully customizable </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Singles, 3, and doubles games </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Split screen </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Network : LAN and online games </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >1 to 6 games per set, in best of 1, 3 or 5 sets </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >7 camera modes </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Moving sun and Night session </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is very Modding-friendly</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Warnings for the Online mode :</strong> </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can play doubles with 4 human players on 1 computer, or on 2 computers with 2 players on each, via LAN or Internet — but not on four separate computers.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Online play uses peer-to-peer (P2P) connections with no relay server. This means that if you're behind CGNAT, or if you cannot forward a UDP port or use UPnP on your Internet router, you won’t be able to host a match. You should still be able to join a host, though.</p></li></ul>",
